::ENG4_U05_L02_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG4.V.02] The root cred relates to belief. In context, what does credibility mean? Sentence: The panel questioned the credibility of the claim because no evidence was provided.
{
~A. The claim's length.#Incorrect. Length is not connected to the root cred or the context.
=B. The claim's trustworthiness.#Correct. Credibility means whether something can be believed or trusted.
~C. The claim's location.#Incorrect. Location is unrelated to the root and context.
~D. The claim's punctuation.#Incorrect. Punctuation is not the meaning of credibility.
}
::ENG4_U05_L02_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Which sentence uses status quo accurately?
{
=A. The proposal challenged the status quo by changing a policy that had existed for years.#Correct. Status quo means the existing state of things.
~B. The proposal created the status quo by introducing something completely new.#Incorrect. Status quo refers to what already exists.
~C. The status quo means a temporary committee.#Incorrect. That meaning fits ad hoc, not status quo.
~D. The status quo means legally required.#Incorrect. That meaning does not fit the phrase.
}
::ENG4_U05_L02_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Sentence: The club had no official leader, but Maya became the de facto organizer. Which paraphrase is accurate?
{
~A. Maya was legally appointed by a court.#Incorrect. De facto means in practice, not necessarily legally.
~B. Maya refused to organize anything.#Incorrect. This contradicts the sentence.
=C. Maya was not officially leader, but she effectively acted as organizer.#Correct. This preserves the phrase's meaning in context.
~D. Maya created a dictionary definition.#Incorrect. This is unrelated.
}
::ENG4_U05_L02_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG4.V.02] The root scribe/script relates to writing. Which word most directly belongs to this family?
{
~A. audible#Incorrect. Audible relates to hearing, not writing.
~B. portable#Incorrect. Portable relates to carrying.
~C. visible#Incorrect. Visible relates to seeing.
=D. transcript#Correct. A transcript is a written record and belongs to the scribe/script family.
}
::ENG4_U05_L02_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG4.V.02] What does ad hoc mean in this sentence? The team formed an ad hoc group to solve the scheduling problem before the deadline.
{
~A. Old and traditional.#Incorrect. That does not fit the context.
=B. Created for a specific purpose or situation.#Correct. The group was formed for the scheduling problem.
~C. Legally required forever.#Incorrect. Ad hoc does not mean permanent or legally required.
~D. Impossible to understand.#Incorrect. The phrase describes the group's purpose, not confusion.
}
